Sometimes, the same IP showed up in over two dozen hits an hour. She and her husband wondered: could it be the same user from Rate My Professors? Sinha then checked his personal website and grew even more alarmed. The same IP address had also been visiting his pages frequently, lingering on his résumé and published writing. Then, in December, police from Southern Connecticut State University contacted Umamaheswar’s department. The chair called Umamaheswar to inform her that a student had filed a police report against her and two other professors on campus. The report noted that she contacted police “regarding a possible hacking of her personal laptop computer which she stated was perpetrated by three faculty members of the Sociology Department,” including Umamaheswar. The student had taken classes with each of the three professors and also accused them “of using students in the class to follow her around and look at her papers which has made her extremely uncomfortable and feel unsafe.” The police report also referred to the student by name.","entities":["Rate My Professors","Southern Connecticut State University","Umamaheswar","the student","Sociology Department","police report","possible hacking of her personal laptop computer","using students in the class to follow her around and look at her papers","The obsessive tormenter who made professors’ lives miserable","Sinha","The Verge"],"facts":["Umamaheswar -WORKS_FOR-> George Mason University","Umamaheswar -PARTICIPATED_IN-> filing police reports","S -SAID-> Umamaheswar","Southern Connecticut State University Police -PART_OF-> Southern Connecticut State University","Umamaheswar -LOCATED_IN-> Connecticut"]}
