PURDY: Has hit at least 20 Fantasy points in 8 of his 9 regular-season starts, and it really should be 9 for 9 because of that first touchdown that was ruled a lateral back in Week 2. If you include the two playoff games he completed, Purdy has delivered at least 20 in 9 of 11 games. And in 5 of those 9 he hit at least 23 Fantasy points including each of his past two games.

COWBOYS: Dallas' defense lost top cornerback Trevon Diggs and they're still red hot. They lead the league in pass rush pressure rate this season (55.6%) and they're in the top-10 in blitz rate (31.9%). It's that pressure that's helped the Cowboys rank in the top-five in completion rate allowed (57.4%), passing touchdowns allowed (two) and missed tackles on pass plays (just five, that's best in football).","entities":["NFL","NFL Fantasy Football Week 5 Lineup Decisions: Starts, Sits, Sleepers, Busts to know for every game","Trevon Diggs","CBSSports.com","fantasy football","Purdy","Cowboys"],"facts":["Brock Purdy -MENTIONS-> NFL","Raiders vs. Lions live score, updates, highlights from NFL 'Monday Night Football' game -MENTIONS-> NFL","Fans spot Travis Kelce wearing Taylor Swift-themed friendship bracelet before she attended his game -MENTIONS-> NFL","Chiefs vs. Packers live score, updates, highlights from NFL 'Sunday Night Football' game -MENTIONS-> NFL","Christmas Day preview: 49ers, Ravens square off in potential Super Bowl sneak peek -MENTIONS-> NFL"]}

